            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Years and Education</strong><br>\nSally Ride was born on May 26, 1951, in Los Angeles, California. She excelled in science and sports from a young age and eventually earned a bachelor's degree in English and physics from Stanford University, followed by a master's and a Ph.D. in physics.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Joining NASA</strong><br>\nIn 1978, Sally Ride was selected as an astronaut candidate by NASA, becoming part of the first class of astronauts to include women. She underwent rigorous training, specializing in the operation of the Space Shuttle's robotic arm.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Historic Spaceflight</strong><br>\nRide became the first American woman to travel to space on June 18, 1983, aboard the Space Shuttle Challenger on the STS-7 mission. She served as a mission specialist and helped deploy two communications satellites.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          }
        ],
        "slideBackgroundSelector": {}
      },
      {
        "elements": [
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 4.415011037527593,
            "width": 37.98882681564246,
            "height": 8.830022075055187,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><span style=\"font-size:1.5em;\"><strong>INFORMATION TEXT (Part 2)</strong></span></p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "55aaf4d3-f7e3-4a3e-9196-01a6f7474f94"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Second Shuttle Flight</strong><br>\nShe flew her second spaceflight in 1984, also on the Challenger, conducting scientific experiments and operating the robotic arm for satellite deployment and other shuttle tasks.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Post-NASA Career</strong><br>\nAfter leaving NASA in 1987, Ride became a physics professor at the University of California, San Diego, and directed the California Space Institute.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Advocacy and Education</strong><br>\nRide founded Sally Ride Science in 2001, an organization aimed at promoting science, technology, engineering, and math (STEM) education, with a particular focus on supporting girls' and young women's interests in these fields.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
